# Tiny Village team coordination (always on)

Full policy: [`docs/agents/team-coordination.md`](../../docs/agents/team-coordination.md).
Root `AGENTS.md` stays the canonical contributor guide; this rule only binds
delegated work to that policy.

- Before substantive delegated work, read `docs/agents/team-coordination.md`
  (routing table §4, assignment template §6, return contract §7, invariants §9).
- The primary session coordinates and is the only repository writer.
  Specialists investigate, review, and propose; they never edit, run commands,
  or repair what they review, and their recommendations are not human
  acceptance.
- Schedule independent investigations concurrently and dependent work in
  order; reconcile conflicting findings against repository evidence.
- Durable human decisions live only in `docs/decisions.md`; resumable task
  context lives in `memory-bank/`. Do not create competing logs.
- If specialist invocation is unavailable, the primary agent performs the
  checks itself and reports plainly that no independent specialist review
  occurred.
